# Rover P4 60 four-door saloon, 1953-1959.
#
# The 2.0-litre six member of the P4 range: the 'Auntie' Rover body with the
# upright grille, the separate wing line and the sloping tail. The 60 was the
# cheaper P4 below the 75 and 90.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rover_P4
#
# Dimensions 4.528 x 1.666 x 1.607 m, wheelbase 2.819 m.
#
# Shape reference: no true level side elevation exists in the pack. Image 1
# is a TAS 393 car identified as a 60, taken from a shallow angle; the flank
# is estimated from that view and the front and rear three-quarters within
# the published dimensions. The limitation is recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (b), the UK P4 Drivers Guild's year-based compilation, not a
# variant-specific factory chart. Black, Sage Green, Dove Grey and Maroon are
# documented Rover finishes of the period. Weights 18, 16, 14, 12, total 60,
# provisional.
#
# Speed 135 km/h. Comfort 60/270, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 60. Classes 3,4.
# Dates are road presence: 1953 intro, retires staggered 1975-1978.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/rover-p4-60.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/rover-p4-60.dae. References:
# citycars/references/rover-p4-60/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: there is no true side elevation; image 1 is shallow
# front-oblique and the flank is estimated from it and the other views. The roof
# corners are too angular, the lamps project too far, and the grille crest is
# simplified. At 128 px the upright P4 cabin, wing line and sloping tail read as
# a P4 60.


obj=citycar
